    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "pb",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 1: an array of n numbers, and a long mix of two operations: the sum from l to r, and setting A of i to a new value. With a plain array, a sum adds up to n elements; an update is instant."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 1 of 7: the range query problem"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "stages"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "pb"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "pb[0]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "With prefix sums, a range sum is one subtraction, but an update changes every later prefix: Theta of n."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "pb[1]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "A segment tree does both in Theta of log n."
